{
 "kind": "skeleton",
 "title": "An editor with its preview",
 "caption": "It stands in a rail, the navigation and the content attached, at the body's full width: the rail stands shut to its icons, and on a phone one bar stands at the top. The page is an entry that is a page, so it is one container, and its header is the page level: the way back, then the title. Its actions stand at the start of its footer. A row of tabs at the top of its content chooses the form of the message, and one save holds every form. Under the tabs the content has a part for the details that have no preview, and then one part for each thing a person writes, under that thing's title. At a desktop the editor stands beside its own result in each part. On a tablet and a phone a person sees the writing or the result, one at a time: a second row of tabs, Write and Result, moves between them, and the choice holds for every part at once. Bars stand for the running text of the message.",
